    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "cmake: Reject warnings in `check_cxx_source_compiles_with_flags()`, use `-msse4.1` for SHA-NI",
    "user": {
      "login": "hebasto",
      "id": 32963518,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTYzNTE4",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32963518?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/hebasto",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/hebasto/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "This is a prerequisite for #31507.\n\n1. We expect that neither the compiler flags nor the test source triggers any warnings, such as `-Wunknown-argument`. Therefore, append `working_compiler_werror_flag`, as done in [`try_append_cxx_flags()`](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/master/cmake/module/TryAppendCXXFlags.cmake).\n\n2. `-msse4` is merely a synonym for `-msse4.2` in both GCC and Clang, but it is not accepted by the clang-cl frontend. Furthermore, the x86 SHA-NI code uses only SSE4.1 intrinsics and no SSE4.2 ones.\n\nReplace `-msse4` with `-msse4.1` to resolve both issues.\n\nThe absence of SSE4.2 usage can be verified by building with `-DAPPEND_CXXFLAGS=-mno-sse4.2`. ",
