        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree c08ce547e5c7d8a87b2a0ab82a33a60378c5a49a\nparent f8e5906015a0681dc60d07fa57cb42acc100d9f6\nauthor Hennadii Stepanov <32963518+hebasto@users.noreply.github.com> 1792156136 +0900\ncommitter Hennadii Stepanov <32963518+hebasto@users.noreply.github.com> 1792156136 +0900\n\ncmake, crypto: Use `-msse4.1` instead of `-msse4` for x86 SHA-NI\n\n`-msse4` is merely a synonym for `-msse4.2` in both GCC and Clang, but\nit is not accepted by the clang-cl frontend. Furthermore, the x86\nSHA-NI code uses only SSE4.1 intrinsics and no SSE4.2 ones.\n\nReplace `-msse4` with `-msse4.1` to resolve both issues.\n\nThe absence of SSE4.2 usage can be verified by building with\n`-DAPPEND_CXXFLAGS=-mno-sse4.2`.\n",
